    "Between 1887 and 1896 Ibrat travelled to Mecca, Medina, Istanbul, Cairo, India and other lands, studying the scripts and languages of many peoples. On his return he published in 1901 “Lughati sitta alsina” (Dictionary of Six Languages), comparing words in Arabic, Persian, Hindi, Turkic, Sart (Uzbek) and Russian. In 1908 he opened the lithographic press “Matbaai Ishoqiya” in To'raqo'rg'on.",
